# Python / tooling caches — never project artefacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.egg-info/
.venv/

# Coverage and test-run outputs
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# Fitted model binaries: fully regenerable from the pinned seeds and the frozen simulator,
# and the repository's convention is to keep generated binaries out of Git.
results/models/*.joblib

# Generated synthetic data IS committed (the deliverable list requires data/synthetic/ CSVs, and
# `tests/test_integration_e2e.py::test_the_committed_dataset_is_what_the_generator_produces_today`
# re-derives every committed row from the frozen simulator, so a stale dataset cannot survive).
#
# The rule that was declared before the files existed, now satisfied: the whole set (5 seeds x
# 4000 rows + 5 x 480 held-out rows + latent factors + metadata) measures 9.5 MiB, under the
# stated 10 MB threshold. The two ignore lines that held this directory empty were removed in
# Phase 3 wave F, exactly as the note here said they would be.

# Hypothesis example database
.hypothesis/
